        "status": "completed",
        "answer": "**Result:** Control recorded 0 conversions from 1000 users, versus 10 from 1000 for treatment. Conversion rates were 0% and 1%, respectively, for an absolute lift of 1 percentage points.\n\nThe improvement is statistically significant under the prespecified treatment-greater-than-control test (p = 0.000954732582670807). The two-sided 95% confidence interval for the absolute lift is 0.4 percentage points to 1.83 percentage points.\n\n**Relative lift is undefined** because it requires dividing by the control conversion rate, which was 0%. With a zero denominator, no finite percentage lift can be calculated.\n\nBecause outcomes were sparse, Fisher’s exact test was used instead of the z approximation. The result supports higher treatment conversion, but experiment validity and practical benefit should be checked before rollout.\n\nStatistical conclusion: Evidence supports higher treatment conversion for the specified test; practical benefit and experiment validity still require review.\n\nTest: Fisher exact, alternative=larger, alpha=0.05. Interval: 95%, two-sided, newcombe_wilson.\nAssumes independent binomial outcomes; randomization and sample-ratio mismatch were not verified. Sparse observed or pooled expected counts: used Fisher exact instead of the z approximation.",
